--- Step 9 ---
Thought: The codebase correctly identifies and handles Facebook Graph API errors with codes 10 (outside 24h window/permission) and 551 (recipient unavailable) as non-retryable, preventing further processing or retries for these specific cases.

However, the system identifies error code 613 as a rate-limiting error in `scripts/check-page-token-health.js`, but there is no specific handling for it in the core message sending logic (e.g., `core/webhook.js` or `core/messenger-send-errors.js`) to implement a backoff strategy or delayed retry. If an error with code 613 occurs during webhook processing, it is re-thrown as a generic error. Without explicit backoff, this could lead to blind retries, exacerbating the rate limit issue.

This constitutes a finding as per the audit requirement: "Nuot chung moi loi hoac retry mu = finding." for rate limit errors.
